#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""event-card: one live card, pinned in the owner's Telegram chat, for an event night (token-free; Bot API direct,
or the live outbox while the live tg-adapter runs).

  event-card run [--dry-run] [--now ISO]   cron, every 2 min. On an event night, from the first leg's departure minus
                                           90 min: send ONE silent message and pin it silently, then edit it every run
                                           until he is home or the cutoff; then a final edit and unpin: the message
                                           stays in the chat as a record (never deleted); with tracks IDed that night
                                           the final edit is the night recap instead (below). Cheap exit (file reads
                                           only; an open recap adds the local `trackid list` + `lists show`) when no
                                           card is due. --dry-run prints the card and the actions; it sends
                                           nothing and writes no state.
  event-card status [--json] [--now ISO]   tonight's event night, its window, the card's message id and phase;
                                          --json also lists missed_legs {train-watch leg id: planned departure}
                                          (legs home he stayed past, last 2 days): drop train-watch notes on them
  event-card off [--now ISO]               end tonight's card now (final edit + unpin) and skip the rest of tonight;
                                           an open night recap is unpinned too

Event night: a timed calcache event (no travel leg, not all-day, not in the home town) with a 🚆/🚌 leg there
(departing up to 6 h before it starts) or a leg home (departing from its start up to 10 h after its end), or, without
legs, a rave/concert by its title (rave/club/concert words or a rave-radar artist, typos too).
Window: the first leg's departure − 90 min (no legs: the event start − 90 min) until the later of the next 04:45 and
the last leg's arrival + 15 min. It ends earlier when `vault ha now --json` says home after he was seen away (or once
the event has started).
Card: line 1 = what the pinned header shows (event, next train or way home; 🔴 on a broken leg); the next leg with live
delay and platform (`train-watch status ID --json`, from 3 h before departure); leave by (a leg from home: the door
departure; else 10 min before); from the event start the next 3 connections home + the last one tonight (`gohome STOP
--json`, STOP = the start stop of the leg home, else the event's town; arrival at the door, a final walk of 5 min or
more as "→ <last stop> 00:57, 🚶 home 01:14"); weather at the venue (open-meteo, 30 min cache);
the update time; one "📞 Talk" button (callback call:talk: telegram-plus runs ~/bin/talk-button and the voice relay
rings him; marked "keep" in buttons.json), which the final edit drops.
Pins: sendMessage + pinChatMessage both with disable_notification; editMessageText never notifies; unpinChatMessage
always names this card's message_id (never unpinAll), so tg-status's pinned board (it pins only its own new messages and
unpins only by id) keeps working. Telegram keeps several pins; the header shows the newest.
Night recap: when the card ends at home or the cutoff and trackid named tracks that night (`trackid list 200 --json`:
an ID whose last identification falls between the card's start and the recap's end), the final edit turns the card into
a recap instead: the event, the way home (home time, plus the connection it most likely was: the planned leg home or a
connection the card showed, arriving at most 40 min before he was home) and the night's tracks (up to 8, linked), with
one "➕ Crate" button (callback rr:crate:tid-…, rave-radar's) per track not yet on the crate list (`lists show crate
--json`). It stays pinned and is re-edited when new IDs come in or a track reaches the crate, until 18:00 on the morning
after (or the next card), then unpinned by id. No IDs at the end: the final edit + unpin; IDs that still come
in before the recap's end turn the (unpinned) record into the recap. The recap only edits: it never sends a new message
(a missing card ends it), so nothing notifies during the sleep-in guard. Its keyboard is marked "keep" in
telegram-plus's buttons.json so he can tap several.
Alerts: a cancelled leg or a delay >= 10 min turns line 1 red. train-watch already writes one inbox note per problem (the
session sends it on), so event-card sends its own ONE normal message for a leg only when train-watch is not covering it:
the problem is not in its noted keys and its last check of that leg is missing or older than 25 min.
One sender: while the live tg-adapter runs (core.tg's gate; switch ~/.config/tg-adapter/direct-event-card
or direct-all = always direct), each Bot API call becomes a row in the live outbox and the adapter sends it: cards,
edits and pins are never held or deduped, an alert is urgent, keyboards are marked "keep" by the adapter; no token is
read. Otherwise, or when the adapter goes away mid-run, the call goes to the Bot API directly.
Files: ~/.local/state/event-card/ (0700): state.json (message id, night key, alert keys, connections home seen tonight;
no titles, except an open recap's event title until it ends), geo.json, weather.json, artists.json caches, log.
Env (tests): EVENT_CARD_DIR, EVENT_CARD_NOW, EVENT_CARD_API + EVENT_CARD_TEST_TOKEN /
EVENT_CARD_TEST_CHAT (a mock Bot API; the real token only goes to api.telegram.org), EVENT_CARD_CALCACHE (events.json),
EVENT_CARD_TW_DIR (train-watch's state dir), EVENT_CARD_TRAIN_WATCH / EVENT_CARD_GOHOME / EVENT_CARD_VAULT /
EVENT_CARD_RAVE_RADAR / EVENT_CARD_TRACKID / EVENT_CARD_LISTS (commands, or "off"), EVENT_CARD_BUTTONS (telegram-plus's
buttons.json, or "off"; with a mock Bot API only when set), EVENT_CARD_TALK ("off" = no Talk button), EVENT_CARD_WEATHER (an open-meteo forecast JSON file, or "off"),
EVENT_CARD_GEO (geocoding URL or "off"). A simulated --now / EVENT_CARD_NOW passes the time on to train-watch and gohome
and skips the vault unless EVENT_CARD_VAULT is set. Tests ~/opt/event-card-tests/run.sh.
"""
import argparse
import datetime as dt
import hashlib
import html
import json
import os
import pwd
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import unicodedata
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
_here = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
for _lib in (os.path.join(pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir, 'bin', 'lib'), os.path.expanduser('~/bin/lib'),
             os.path.join(_here, 'lib')):
    sys.path.insert(0, _lib)                              # own lib dir first; ~/bin/lib for a copy elsewhere
if not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(_here, 'lib', 'core')) and os.path.isdir(os.path.join(_here, '..', 'core')):
    sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(_here))            # the repo checkout (scripts/): its own core
from core import drive as drive_rule, http as web, jsonstate, locks, tg as tgout  # noqa: E402
import assistant_profile as profile  # noqa: E402

HOME = os.path.expanduser('~')
TZ = profile.tz()
DIR = os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_DIR') or os.path.join(HOME, '.local/state/event-card')
STATE_F = os.path.join(DIR, 'state.json')
CAL_F = os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_CALCACHE') or os.path.join(HOME, '.local/state/calcache/events.json')
TW_DIR = os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_TW_DIR') or os.path.join(HOME, '.local/state/trains')
TG_DIR = os.path.join(HOME, '.claude/channels/telegram')
REAL_API = 'https://api.telegram.org'
API = os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_API') or REAL_API
# The live card's "📞 Talk" button: callback call:talk, run by telegram-plus as an instant button (callbacks.json →
# ~/bin/talk-button: the voice relay rings him). EVENT_CARD_TALK=off hides it. The final edit and the recap drop it.
TALK = (os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_TALK') or 'on').strip().lower() not in ('0', 'off', 'no', 'false')
TALK_MARKUP = {'inline_keyboard': [[{'text': '📞 Talk', 'callback_data': 'call:talk'}]]}


def talk_markup():
    return TALK_MARKUP if TALK else None
LEAD = dt.timedelta(minutes=90)
CUTOFF = dt.time(4, 45)
AFTER_ARR = dt.timedelta(minutes=15)
OUT_WINDOW, BACK_WINDOW = dt.timedelta(hours=6), dt.timedelta(hours=10)
LIVE_FROM = dt.timedelta(hours=3)      # train-watch's own window
BUFFER = dt.timedelta(minutes=10)      # leave by, for a leg that doesn't start at the door
ALERT_DELAY = 10
TW_STALE = dt.timedelta(minutes=25)
WEATHER_TTL = 30 * 60
RAVE_RE = re.compile(r'\brave|\bclub|techno|festival|open[- ]?air|afterhour|warehouse|boiler room|concert|konzert'
                     r'|\bgig\b|\blive\b|\btour\b|\bdj\b', re.I)
TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r'\b\d{6,12}:[A-Za-z0-9_-]{30,}\b')
RAVE_GRACE = dt.timedelta(hours=3)        # a live rave-only night is still found after its cutoff: ends as 'cutoff'
RECAP_UNTIL = dt.time(18, 0)               # the recap stays pinned until 18:00 on the morning after
RECAP_MAX = 8                              # tracks listed (and ➕ buttons) on the recap
RECAP_MATCH = dt.timedelta(minutes=40)     # a connection home counts as taken: it arrives ≤ 40 min before home
DRY = False
SIMULATED = False
LAST_GH = None                             # the last gohome answer render() used (the recap's way home)
LAST_PLACE = None                          # this run's `vault ha now` answer (None: no place source)
MISSED_KEEP = dt.timedelta(days=2)         # missed legs stay listed in state (and status --json) this long
WALK_SHOW = 5                              # a final walk this long (gohome's walk_min) is named on the line
MISSED_GRACE = dt.timedelta(minutes=5)     # still in the venue town this long after the leg home left = missed it
MOVING = {'vehicle', 'bicycle', 'in_vehicle', 'on_bicycle', 'driving'}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ small helpers
def fixed(t):
    """Owner wall time with a fixed UTC offset. Two times in one ZoneInfo subtract and compare as wall clocks (the
    fold is ignored), so in the repeated autumn hour a leg that left at 02:08 CEST looked due again at 02:00 CET; with
    fixed offsets all arithmetic is real elapsed time. Display goes through hm() (back to his zone)."""
    t = t.astimezone(TZ)
    return t.replace(tzinfo=dt.timezone(t.utcoffset()))


def iso(s):
    if not s:
        return None
    try:
        t = dt.datetime.fromisoformat(str(s).strip().replace('Z', '+00:00'))
    except ValueError:
        return None
    return fixed(t.replace(tzinfo=TZ) if t.tzinfo is None else t)


def hm(t):
    return t.astimezone(TZ).strftime('%H:%M')


def until(t, now):
    m = int((t - now).total_seconds() // 60)
    if m < 1:
        return 'now'
    return f'in {m // 60} h {m % 60:02d}' if m >= 60 else f'in {m} min'


def esc(s):
    return html.escape(str(s), quote=False)


def plain(text):
    return html.unescape(re.sub(r'</?[a-z][^>]*>', '', text))


def log(msg):
    if DRY:
        return
    os.makedirs(DIR, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    with open(os.path.join(DIR, 'log'), 'a') as f:
        f.write('%s %s\n' % (dt.datetime.now(TZ).strftime('%F %T'), TOKEN_RE.sub('<token>', msg)))


def read_json(path, default=None):
    return jsonstate.load(path, default)          # missing, unreadable or broken = default (core.jsonstate)


def write_json(path, obj):
    if DRY:
        return
    jsonstate.save(path, obj, mode=0o600, dir_mode=0o700, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)


def cmd_of(env, default):
    v = os.environ.get(env)
    if v == 'off':
        return None
    return v or default


def run_json(argv, extra_env=None, timeout=60):
    env = dict(os.environ, **(extra_env or {}))
    try:
        r = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, env=env)
        return json.loads(r.stdout) if r.returncode == 0 and r.stdout.strip() else None
    except (OSError, ValueError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None


def is_home_place(s):
    try:
        import home_place
        return home_place.is_home(s)
    except Exception:
        return str(s or '').strip().casefold() == 'home'


def home_towns():
    names = [profile.get('home.town', '')] + list(profile.get('home.town_aliases', []) or [])
    return {str(n).strip().casefold() for n in names if n}


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ event nights
def load_events():
    d = read_json(CAL_F, {})
    ev = d.get('events', d) if isinstance(d, dict) else d
    if isinstance(ev, dict):
        ev = list(ev.values())
    out = []
    for e in ev if isinstance(ev, list) else []:
        if isinstance(e, dict) and iso(e.get('start')) and iso(e.get('end')):
            out.append(dict(e, _s=iso(e['start']), _e=iso(e['end'])))
    return sorted(out, key=lambda e: e['_s'])


def rave_artists():
    cache = os.path.join(DIR, 'artists.json')
    c = read_json(cache, {})
    if isinstance(c, dict) and time.time() - c.get('at', 0) < 12 * 3600:
        return c.get('names', [])
    bin_ = cmd_of('EVENT_CARD_RAVE_RADAR', os.path.join(HOME, 'bin/rave-radar'))
    rows = run_json([bin_, 'artists', 'list', '--json'], timeout=15) if bin_ and os.path.exists(bin_) else None
    names = []
    for a in rows if isinstance(rows, list) else []:
        if isinstance(a, dict):
            names += [n.strip().lower() for n in [a.get('name'), *(a.get('aliases') or [])]
                      if isinstance(n, str) and len(n.strip()) >= 3]
    if rows is not None:
        write_json(cache, {'at': time.time(), 'names': names})
    return names


def artist_hit(text, names):
    import difflib
    low = text.lower()
    toks = re.findall(r"[\w'&.-]+", low)
    for n in names:
        if re.search(r'(?<!\w)' + re.escape(n) + r'(?!\w)', low):
            return True
        k = len(n.split())
        if len(n) >= 6 and any(difflib.SequenceMatcher(None, ' '.join(toks[i:i + k]), n).ratio() >= 0.85
                               for i in range(len(toks) - k + 1)):
            return True
    return False


def next_cutoff(t):
    """The next CUTOFF wall time after t (set on his wall clock, so 04:45 stays 04:45 across a clock change)."""
    c = t.astimezone(TZ).replace(hour=CUTOFF.hour, minute=CUTOFF.minute, second=0, microsecond=0, fold=0)
    return fixed(c) if fixed(c) > t else fixed(c + dt.timedelta(days=1))


def find_nights(events, now, rave_check=True):
    """Every event night in the cache: {key, ev, legs (sorted), back (leg home or None), start, end}."""
    legs = [e for e in events if isinstance(e.get('train'), dict) and (e.get('flags') or {}).get('travel') in
            ('train', 'bus')]
    towns = home_towns()
    nights = []
    for m in events:
        fl = m.get('flags') or {}
        if m.get('all_day') or fl.get('travel') or isinstance(m.get('train'), dict):
            continue
        if str(m.get('town') or '').strip().casefold() in towns:
            continue
        s, e = m['_s'], m['_e']
        out = [g for g in legs if s - OUT_WINDOW <= g['_s'] <= s and not is_home_place(g['train'].get('to'))]
        back = [g for g in legs if s <= g['_s'] <= e + BACK_WINDOW and is_home_place(g['train'].get('to'))]
        mine = sorted(out[-1:] + back[:1], key=lambda g: g['_s'])
        if mine:
            start = mine[0]['_s'] - LEAD
        else:
            start = s - LEAD
            if not (rave_check and start <= now < next_cutoff(s) + RAVE_GRACE and
                    (RAVE_RE.search(m.get('title') or '') or artist_hit(m.get('title') or '', rave_artists()))):
                continue
        end = max([next_cutoff(max(s, start + LEAD))] + [g['_e'] + AFTER_ARR for g in mine])
        nights.append({'key': '%s@%s' % (m.get('id'), s.date().isoformat()), 'ev': m, 'legs': mine,
                       'back': back[0] if back else None, 'start': start, 'end': end})
    return nights


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ live sources
def tw_leg_ids():
    d = read_json(os.path.join(TW_DIR, 'legs.json'), {})
    rows = d.get('legs', d) if isinstance(d, dict) else d
    return {r.get('event_id'): r.get('id') for r in rows if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get('event_id')} \
        if isinstance(rows, list) else {}


def tw_status(leg_id, now):
    bin_ = cmd_of('EVENT_CARD_TRAIN_WATCH', os.path.join(HOME, 'bin/train-watch'))
    if not bin_ or not leg_id:
        return None
    env = {'TRAIN_WATCH_NOW': now.isoformat()} if SIMULATED else None
    return run_json([bin_, 'status', leg_id, '--json'], env)


def tw_covers(leg_id, keys, now):
    """True when train-watch is on this problem: noted already, or it checked the leg in the last 25 min."""
    st = (read_json(os.path.join(TW_DIR, 'state.json'), {}) or {}).get('legs', {}).get(leg_id) or {}
    if set(keys) & set(st.get('noted') or []):
        return True
    last = iso(st.get('last'))
    return bool(last and now - last <= TW_STALE)


def go_home(stop, now):
    bin_ = cmd_of('EVENT_CARD_GOHOME', os.path.join(HOME, 'bin/gohome'))
    if not bin_ or not stop:
        return None
    env = {'GOHOME_NOW': now.astimezone(TZ).strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')} if SIMULATED else None
    return run_json([bin_, stop, '--json'], env)


def place_info():
    """`vault ha now --json` (place, drive, activity), or None."""
    default = None if SIMULATED else os.path.join(HOME, 'bin/vault')
    bin_ = cmd_of('EVENT_CARD_VAULT', default)
    if not bin_:
        return None
    d = run_json([bin_, 'ha', 'now', '--json'], timeout=40)
    return d if isinstance(d, dict) and isinstance(d.get('place'), dict) else None


def place_kind(d):
    return d['place'].get('kind') if d else None


def norm(s):
    s = unicodedata.normalize('NFKD', str(s or '')).encode('ascii', 'ignore').decode().casefold()
    return ' '.join(s.replace('-', ' ').replace(',', ' ').split())


def still_here(d, m):
    """True: in the event's town and not moving; False: moving or in another town; None: can't say."""
    if not d:
        return None
    pl = d['place']
    if pl.get('kind') == 'home' or drive_rule.active(d) or \
            str(d.get('activity') or '').casefold() in MOVING:
        return False
    a, t = norm(pl.get('town')), norm(m.get('town'))
    if not a or not t:
        return None
    return a == t or a.startswith(t + ' ') or t.startswith(a + ' ')


def riding(conns, now, since=None):
    """The remembered connection home he is most likely on: left after he was last seen at the venue (since), not
    arrived yet; the latest such one. None when none fits."""
    best = None
    for c in (conns or {}).values():
        d, a = iso(c.get('dep')), iso(c.get('arr'))
        if d and a and d <= now < a and (since is None or d >= since - dt.timedelta(minutes=2)) and \
                (best is None or d > iso(best['dep'])):
            best = c
    return best


URLLIB_UA = 'Python-urllib/%d.%d' % sys.version_info[:2]   # the UA the Bot API calls always sent


def http_json(url, timeout=15):
    with web.open(url, headers={'User-Agent': 'event-card/1'}, timeout=timeout) as r:
        return json.loads(r.read().decode())


def geocode(town):
    cache_f = os.path.join(DIR, 'geo.json')
    cache = read_json(cache_f, {}) or {}
    if town in cache:
        return cache[town]
    base = os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_GEO') or 'https://geocoding-api.open-meteo.com/v1/search'
    if base == 'off':
        return None
    try:
        res = http_json(base + '?' + urllib.parse.urlencode({'name': town, 'count': 5, 'format': 'json'}))
    except Exception:
        return None
    rows = [r for r in res.get('results') or [] if 'latitude' in r]
    if not rows:
        return None
    hl, ho = profile.get('home.lat', None), profile.get('home.lon', None)
    if hl is not None and ho is not None:   # the one nearest home (Bern CH, not Bern US)
        rows.sort(key=lambda r: (r['latitude'] - float(hl)) ** 2 + (r['longitude'] - float(ho)) ** 2)
    cache[town] = [round(rows[0]['latitude'], 3), round(rows[0]['longitude'], 3)]
    write_json(cache_f, cache)
    return cache[town]


WMO = ((0, '☀️'), (2, '🌤'), (3, '☁️'), (48, '🌫'), (57, '🌦'), (67, '🌧'), (77, '🌨'), (82, '🌧'), (86, '🌨'), (99, '⛈'))


def weather_line(town, a, b):
    """'🌧 Zürich 19–22 h: 9–7°, rain 60 %' for the hours a..b (local), or None."""
    if not town:
        return None
    fix = os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_WEATHER')
    if fix == 'off':
        return None
    key = '%s|%s' % (town, a.date().isoformat())
    if fix:
        data = read_json(fix)
    else:
        cache_f = os.path.join(DIR, 'weather.json')
        cache = read_json(cache_f, {}) or {}
        c = cache.get(key)
        if c and time.time() - c.get('at', 0) < WEATHER_TTL:
            data = c['data']
        else:
            ll = geocode(town)
            if not ll:
                return None
            q = {'latitude': ll[0], 'longitude': ll[1], 'timezone': str(TZ),
                 'hourly': 'temperature_2m,precipitation_probability,weather_code',
                 'start_date': a.date().isoformat(), 'end_date': (b.date() + dt.timedelta(days=0)).isoformat()}
            try:
                data = http_json('https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?' + urllib.parse.urlencode(q))
            except Exception:
                return None
            cache = {k: v for k, v in cache.items() if time.time() - v.get('at', 0) < 86400}
            cache[key] = {'at': time.time(), 'data': data}
            write_json(cache_f, cache)
    h = (data or {}).get('hourly') or {}
    rows = []
    for i, t in enumerate(h.get('time') or []):
        tt = fixed(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(t).replace(tzinfo=TZ))
        if a.replace(minute=0, second=0, microsecond=0) <= tt <= b:
            try:
                rows.append((tt, h['temperature_2m'][i], (h.get('precipitation_probability') or [0] * 999)[i] or 0,
                             h['weather_code'][i]))
            except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError):
                pass
    rows = [r for r in rows if r[1] is not None]
    if not rows:
        return None
    temps = [r[1] for r in rows]
    rain = max(r[2] for r in rows)
    code = max(r[3] or 0 for r in rows)
    emo = next((e for lim, e in WMO if code <= lim), '🌡')
    if code <= 1 and not 7 <= rows[0][0].hour < 19:
        emo = '🌙'
    t0, t1 = round(temps[0]), round(temps[-1])
    span = f'{t0}°' if t0 == t1 else f'{t0}–{t1}°'
    hrs = f'{rows[0][0].hour}–{rows[-1][0].hour} h' if len(rows) > 1 else f'{rows[0][0].hour} h'
    return f'{emo} {town} {hrs}: {span}' + (f', rain {rain} %' if rain >= 20 else '')


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ the card
def leg_route(g):
    t = g['train']
    f = 'home' if is_home_place(t.get('from')) else t.get('from') or '?'
    to = 'home' if is_home_place(t.get('to')) else t.get('to') or '?'
    return f'{f} → {to}'


def leg_lines(g, live=None):
    ls = (live or {}).get('lines') or g['train'].get('lines') or []
    return ' '.join(ls[:3]) + (' …' if len(ls) > 3 else '')


def leg_block(g, now, live, problem):
    """(head bit, card lines) for the next leg."""
    dep, arr = g['_s'], g['_e']
    lines_ = leg_lines(g, live)
    plat = (live or {}).get('platform')
    pl = f' · pl {esc(plat)}' if plat else ''
    if problem:
        state = '❌ cancelled' if problem == 'cancel' else f"🔴 +{live['delay']} min"
    elif live:
        state = 'on time' if not live.get('delay') else f"+{live['delay']} min"
    else:
        state = 'planned'
    if now >= dep:   # on board
        eta = arr + dt.timedelta(minutes=(live or {}).get('delay') or 0)
        head = f'🚆 {lines_} → {"home" if is_home_place(g["train"].get("to")) else esc(g["train"].get("to"))} {hm(eta)}'
        return head, [f'🚆 On the way: {esc(lines_)} {esc(leg_route(g))}, arrives {hm(eta)}'
                      + (f' ({state})' if live else '')]
    out = [f'🚆 Next: {hm(dep)} {esc(lines_)} {esc(leg_route(g))}{pl} · {state}']
    if problem and live and (live.get('text') or '').strip():
        out.append(f'   live: {esc(live["text"])}')
    alt = (live or {}).get('alt') if problem else None
    if alt:
        link = alt.get('link')
        t = esc(alt.get('text') or '')
        out.append('   ↪ ' + (f'<a href="{esc(link)}">{t}</a>' if link else t))
    if is_home_place(g['train'].get('from')):
        lb = dep
        out.append(f'🚶 Leave by {hm(lb)} ({until(lb, now)})')
    else:
        lb = dep - BUFFER
        out.append(f'🚶 Leave for {esc(g["train"].get("from"))} by {hm(lb)} ({until(lb, now)})')
    if is_home_place(g['train'].get('from')):   # a door leg: the header says when to leave
        head = f'🚶 leave {hm(dep)} · {plain(state)}'
    else:
        head = f'🚆 {lines_} {hm(dep)}' + (f' pl {plat}' if plat else '') + f' · {plain(state)}'
    return head, out


def conn_line(c, tag=''):
    t = fixed(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(c['dep']))
    a = fixed(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(c['arr']))
    dep = f'<a href="{esc(c["link"])}">{hm(t)}</a>' if c.get('link') else hm(t)
    ls = ' '.join((c.get('lines') or [])[:3])
    pl = f' pl {esc(c["platform"])}' if c.get('platform') else ''
    ch = f' · {c["changes"]}×' if c.get('changes') else ''
    w, off, oa = c.get('walk_min'), c.get('off'), c.get('off_arr')
    if isinstance(w, int) and w >= WALK_SHOW and off and oa:   # gohome's arr is at the door: name a long last mile
        oa = fixed(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(oa))
        return f'{tag}{dep} {esc(ls)}{pl} → {esc(off)} {hm(oa)}, 🚶 home {hm(a)}{ch}'
    return f'{tag}{dep} {esc(ls)}{pl} → {hm(a)}{ch}'


def home_block(gh, now, night_end):
    """(head bit, lines) from gohome --json. A 'last' after the card's window belongs to the next night: dropped."""
    if not isinstance(gh, dict):
        return None, ['🏠 Way home: not checked (/gohome)']
    if gh.get('home'):
        return None, []
    nxt, last = gh.get('next') or [], gh.get('last')
    ld = fixed(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(last['dep'])) if last and last.get('dep') else None
    if ld and ld > night_end:
        last, ld = None, None
    if not nxt and not last:
        return None, ['🏠 No connection home found (/gohome)']
    last_dep = last and last.get('dep')
    out = [f'🏠 Home from {esc(gh.get("origin") or "?")}:']
    for c in nxt[:3]:
        out.append('   ' + conn_line(c, '🌙 ' if c.get('dep') == last_dep else ''))
    head = '🏠 next ' + hm(dt.datetime.fromisoformat(nxt[0]['dep'])) if nxt else '🏠'
    if ld and last_dep not in [c.get('dep') for c in nxt[:3]]:
        out.append(('🌙 Last ' + conn_line(last)) if ld > now else f'🌙 Last one left at {hm(ld)}')
    if ld and ld > now:
        head += f' · last {hm(ld)}'
    return head, out


def problem_of(live):
    if not live or not isinstance(live.get('live'), dict) and not live.get('problems'):
        return None
    lv = live.get('live') or {}
    if lv.get('cancelled') or any('cancel' in str(p.get('key', '')) or 'gone' in str(p.get('key', ''))
                                  for p in live.get('problems') or []):
        return 'cancel'
    if (lv.get('delay') or 0) >= ALERT_DELAY:
        return 'delay'
    return None


def render(n, now, tw_ids, missed=False, here=None, conns=None, here_at=None):
    """missed: he stayed in the venue town past the leg home's departure (the card then keeps the way home and
    never claims he is on that leg); here: still_here() of this run; conns: the remembered connections home."""
    global LAST_GH
    LAST_GH = None
    m, legs = n['ev'], n['legs']
    title = (m.get('title') or 'Event').strip()
    nxt = next((g for g in legs if (g['_e'] or g['_s']) > now), None)
    head_bits, body, alert = [], [], None
    back = n.get('back')
    missed_leg = bool(missed and back is not None and now >= back['_s'])
    if nxt and missed_leg and nxt.get('id') == back.get('id'):
        nxt = None                                # not his train any more
    if nxt:
        st = None
        lid = tw_ids.get(nxt.get('id'))
        if nxt['_s'] - LIVE_FROM <= now <= nxt['_e']:
            st = tw_status(lid, now)
        live = dict((st or {}).get('live') or {}, alt=(st or {}).get('alt')) if st and st.get('live') else None
        prob = problem_of(st)
        if prob == 'cancel' and live is None:
            live = {'cancelled': True, 'alt': (st or {}).get('alt')}
        hb, lines_ = leg_block(nxt, now, live, prob)
        if prob:
            alert = {'leg': lid, 'kind': prob, 'keys': [p.get('key') for p in st.get('problems') or []],
                     'line': plain(lines_[0]), 'alt': (st or {}).get('alt')}
        head_bits.append(hb)
        body += lines_
    if missed_leg:
        c = riding(conns, now, here_at) if here is False else None
        if c:
            ls = esc(' '.join(c.get('lines') or []) or 'train')
            head_bits.append(f'🚆 {plain(ls)} → home {hm(iso(c["arr"]))}')
            body.append(f'🚆 On the way (likely): {ls} {hm(iso(c["dep"]))}'
                        + (f' from {esc(c["from"])}' if c.get('from') else '') + f', arrives {hm(iso(c["arr"]))}')
        elif here is not False:
            body.append(f'🚆 Planned {hm(back["_s"])} {esc(leg_lines(back))} left without you')
    started = now >= m['_s']
    on_way_home = back is not None and now >= back['_s'] and not (missed_leg and here is not False)
    if started and not on_way_home:
        stop = back['train'].get('from') if back else m.get('town')
        LAST_GH = go_home(stop, now)
        hb, lines_ = home_block(LAST_GH, now, n["end"])
        if hb and not alert:                     # the header: the way home once the event is on, a broken leg first
            head_bits = [hb]
        body += lines_
    wl = weather_line(m.get('town'), max(now, m['_s'] - dt.timedelta(hours=1)),
                      min(m['_e'], max(now, m['_s']) + dt.timedelta(hours=6)))
    if wl:
        body.append(wl)
    when = f'{hm(m["_s"])}–{hm(m["_e"])}'
    top = ('🔴 ' if alert else '🎟 ') + esc(title) + (' · ' + esc(head_bits[0]) if head_bits else f' · {when}')
    text = '\n'.join([f'<b>{top}</b>', f'📍 {esc(m.get("town") or "?")} · {when}'] + body
                     + [f'<i>🕑 live · {hm(now)}</i>'])
    return text, alert


def final_text(n, now, why):
    m = n['ev']
    title = esc((m.get('title') or 'Event').strip())
    legs = ' · '.join(f'{hm(g["_s"])}→{hm(g["_e"])}' for g in n['legs'])
    first = {'home': f'✅ {title} · home {hm(now)}', 'off': f'⏹ {title} · live card stopped {hm(now)}',
             'gone': f'⏹ {title} · no longer in the calendar'}.get(why, f'🌙 {title} · live card ended {hm(now)}')
    return '\n'.join([f'<b>{first}</b>'] + ([f'🚆 {legs}'] if legs else []) + ['<i>Live card ended; kept as a record.</i>'])


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ Telegram
class TgError(Exception):
    def __init__(self, code, desc):
        super().__init__('%s %s' % (code, desc))
        self.code, self.desc = code, desc


_creds = None


def creds():
    global _creds
    if _creds:
        return _creds
    if API != REAL_API:   # a test server never gets the real token
        _creds = (os.environ['EVENT_CARD_TEST_TOKEN'], os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_TEST_CHAT', '1'))
        return _creds
    tok = None
    with open(os.path.join(TG_DIR, '.env')) as f:
        for ln in f:
            k, _, v = ln.strip().partition('=')
            if k.strip().replace('export ', '') == 'TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN':
                tok = v.strip().strip('"\'')
    with open(os.path.join(TG_DIR, 'access.json')) as f:
        chat = str(json.load(f)['allowFrom'][0])
    if not tok:
        raise RuntimeError('no bot token')
    _creds = (tok, chat)
    return _creds


_OUTBOX = None


def outbox():
    """One sender: True = this run's Bot API calls go through the live outbox (core.tg; the live tg-adapter sends
    them, holding no card and deduping nothing; alerts are urgent), decided once per run: while the live adapter runs
    and ~/.config/tg-adapter/direct-event-card (or direct-all) is absent. Never with a test API (EVENT_CARD_API)."""
    global _OUTBOX
    if _OUTBOX is None:
        _OUTBOX = False
        if API == REAL_API and not DRY:
            try:
                _OUTBOX = tgout.outbox_on('event-card')[0]
            except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 (the direct path is the safe default)
                log('outbox gate: %s' % type(e).__name__)
    return _OUTBOX


def call(method, **params):
    if outbox():
        mk = params.get('reply_markup') or {}
        try:
            return tgout.bot_call(method, params, sender='event-card', hold=False, dedupe=False,
                                  urgent=method == 'sendMessage' and not params.get('disable_notification'),
                                  on_press='keep' if mk.get('inline_keyboard') else None)
        except tgout.TgError as e:
            if e.code != -1:
                raise TgError(e.code, TOKEN_RE.sub('<token>', e.desc))
            log('outbox: %s; direct path' % e.desc)   # the live adapter went away: the direct call below
    tok, chat = creds()
    params.setdefault('chat_id', chat)
    try:
        with web.open('%s/bot%s/%s' % (API, tok, method), json.dumps(params).encode(),
                      headers={'Content-Type': 'application/json'}, timeout=15, ua=URLLIB_UA) as r:
            body = json.loads(r.read().decode())
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        try:
            body = json.loads(e.read().decode())
        except Exception:
            body = {'ok': False, 'error_code': e.code, 'description': 'HTTP %s' % e.code}
    except Exception as e:   # never let a URL (with the token) reach a log
        raise TgError(0, TOKEN_RE.sub('<token>', '%s: %s' % (type(e).__name__, e)))
    if not body.get('ok'):
        raise TgError(body.get('error_code', 0), TOKEN_RE.sub('<token>', str(body.get('description', ''))))
    return body.get('result')


def send_card(text):
    mk = {'reply_markup': talk_markup()} if talk_markup() else {}
    try:
        m = call('sendMessage', text=text, parse_mode='HTML', disable_notification=True,
                 link_preview_options={'is_disabled': True}, **mk)
    except TgError as e:
        if "can't parse entities" not in e.desc.lower():
            raise
        m = call('sendMessage', text=plain(text), disable_notification=True,
                 link_preview_options={'is_disabled': True}, **mk)
    return m['message_id']


def pin(mid):
    try:
        call('pinChatMessage', message_id=mid, disable_notification=True)
    except TgError as e:
        log('pin failed: %s' % e.desc)


def unpin(mid):
    try:
        call('unpinChatMessage', message_id=mid)
    except TgError as e:
        log('unpin %s: %s' % (mid, e.desc))


def edit(mid, text, markup=None):
    """True = edited (or unchanged); False = the message is gone (send a new one). markup: an inline keyboard."""
    for t, mode in ((text, 'HTML'), (plain(text), None)):
        try:
            call('editMessageText', message_id=mid, text=t, link_preview_options={'is_disabled': True},
                 **({'parse_mode': mode} if mode else {}), **({'reply_markup': markup} if markup else {}))
            return True
        except TgError as e:
            d = e.desc.lower()
            if 'not modified' in d:
                return True
            if mode and "can't parse entities" in d:
                continue
            if 'message to edit not found' in d or "can't be edited" in d or 'message_id_invalid' in d:
                return False
            raise
    return True


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ night recap
def remember_conns(st, gh):
    """Keep the connections home the card showed tonight (dep, arr, lines, from): the recap's way home."""
    if not isinstance(gh, dict) or gh.get('home'):
        return
    seen = st.setdefault('conns', {})
    for c in (gh.get('next') or [])[:3] + ([gh['last']] if isinstance(gh.get('last'), dict) else []):
        if isinstance(c, dict) and iso(c.get('dep')) and iso(c.get('arr')):
            seen[c['dep']] = {'dep': c['dep'], 'arr': c['arr'], 'lines': list(c.get('lines') or [])[:3],
                              'from': gh.get('origin')}
    st['conns'] = dict(sorted(seen.items(), key=lambda kv: iso(kv[0]))[-16:])


def night_hits(since, until):
    """trackid IDs last identified in [since, until), oldest first; None when trackid can't say."""
    bin_ = cmd_of('EVENT_CARD_TRACKID', os.path.join(HOME, 'bin/trackid'))
    if not bin_:
        return []
    rows = run_json([bin_, 'list', '200', '--json'], timeout=30)
    if not isinstance(rows, list):
        return None
    out = []
    for r in rows:
        t = iso(r.get('ts')) if isinstance(r, dict) else None
        if t and since <= t < until and str(r.get('id') or '').startswith('tid-') and r.get('crate'):
            out.append(dict(r, _t=t))
    return sorted(out, key=lambda r: r['_t'])


def crate_key(s):
    return ' '.join(re.sub(r'\s*[–—-]\s*', ' - ', str(s or '')).casefold().split())


def crate_items():
    """The crate list's items (open and checked) as crate_key()s; None when lists can't say (then every ➕ shows)."""
    bin_ = cmd_of('EVENT_CARD_LISTS', os.path.join(HOME, 'bin/lists'))
    d = run_json([bin_, 'show', 'crate', '--json'], timeout=20) if bin_ else None
    if not isinstance(d, dict):
        return None
    items = list(d.get('open') or []) + list(d.get('done') or [])
    return {crate_key(x.get('text') if isinstance(x, dict) else x) for x in items} - {''}


def new_recap(st, n, now, why):
    m = n['ev']
    until = max(fixed(dt.datetime.combine(next_cutoff(m['_s']).date(), RECAP_UNTIL, tzinfo=TZ)),
                now + dt.timedelta(hours=2))
    conns = list((st.get('conns') or {}).values())
    b = n.get('back')
    if b and not is_home_place(b['train'].get('from')):
        conns.append({'dep': b['_s'].isoformat(), 'arr': b['_e'].isoformat(),
                      'lines': list(b['train'].get('lines') or [])[:3], 'from': b['train'].get('from')})
    return {'night': n['key'], 'message_id': st.get('message_id'), 'title': (m.get('title') or 'Event').strip(),
            'town': m.get('town'), 'ev_start': m['_s'].isoformat(), 'since': n['start'].isoformat(),
            'until': until.isoformat(), 'home_at': now.isoformat() if why == 'home' else None,
            'conns': conns[-17:], 'pinned': False, 'hash': None}


def way_home(rc):
    """'🏠 Home 02:31 · 🚆 S9 01:45 from X → 02:24' (the connection that most likely got him home), or None."""
    home = iso(rc.get('home_at'))
    if not home:
        return None
    best = None
    for c in rc.get('conns') or []:
        d, a = iso(c.get('dep')), iso(c.get('arr'))
        if d and a and home - RECAP_MATCH <= a <= home + dt.timedelta(minutes=5) and (best is None or a > best[1]):
            best = (d, a, c)
    if not best:
        return f'🏠 Home {hm(home)}'
    d, a, c = best
    frm = f' from {esc(c["from"])}' if c.get('from') else ''
    return f'🏠 Home {hm(home)} · 🚆 {esc(" ".join(c.get("lines") or []) or "train")} {hm(d)}{frm} → {hm(a)}'


def recap_text(rc, hits, crate):
    """(HTML text, inline keyboard or None). Line 1 is what the pinned header shows."""
    n = len(hits)
    lines = [f'<b>🌙 {esc(rc.get("title") or "Event")} · {n} track{"" if n == 1 else "s"} IDed</b>']
    s = iso(rc.get('ev_start'))
    if s:
        lines.append(f'📍 {esc(rc.get("town") or "?")} · {s.astimezone(TZ).strftime("%a %d.%m")} {hm(s)}')
    wh = way_home(rc)
    if wh:
        lines.append(wh)
    rows = []
    for i, r in enumerate(hits[:RECAP_MAX], 1):
        url = r.get('deezer_url') or r.get('shazam_url')
        name = (f'<a href="{html.escape(str(url), quote=True)}">{esc(r["crate"])}</a>' if url else esc(r['crate']))
        have = crate is not None and crate_key(r['crate']) in crate
        lines.append(f'{i}. {hm(r["_t"])} {name}' + (' · ✓ crate' if have else ''))
        if not have:
            label = f'➕ {i}. {r.get("title") or r["crate"]}'
            rows.append([{'text': label if len(label) <= 32 else label[:31] + '…',
                          'callback_data': 'rr:crate:' + r['id']}])
    if n > RECAP_MAX:
        lines.append(f'… and {n - RECAP_MAX} more')
    lines.append('<i>Night recap' + (' · ➕ puts a track on your crate list</i>' if rows else '</i>'))
    return '\n'.join(lines), ({'inline_keyboard': rows} if rows else None)


def keep_buttons(mid):
    """Mark a keyboard "keep" in telegram-plus's buttons.json (the recap's ➕ buttons, the live card's Talk)."""
    path = os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_BUTTONS')
    if DRY or path == 'off' or (not path and API != REAL_API) or outbox():   # outbox: the adapter marks it (on_press)
        return
    path = path or os.path.join(os.environ.get('TELEGRAM_STATE_DIR') or TG_DIR, 'buttons.json')
    try:
        d = read_json(path, {})
        d = d if isinstance(d, dict) else {}
        d['%s:%s' % (creds()[1], mid)] = {'on_press': 'keep', 'ts': int(time.time() * 1000)}
        tmp = '%s.tmp%d' % (path, os.getpid())
        fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
        with os.fdopen(fd, 'w') as f:
            json.dump(d, f)
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except (OSError, RuntimeError, KeyError, ValueError) as e:
        log('keep buttons %s: %s' % (mid, type(e).__name__))


def recap_show(rc, hits, why):
    """Edit the card into the recap when it changed. False = the card is gone (the recap ends: never a new message)."""
    text, markup = recap_text(rc, hits, crate_items())
    h = hashlib.sha256((text + json.dumps(markup)).encode()).hexdigest()[:16]
    if h == rc.get('hash'):
        return True
    mid = rc['message_id']
    act(f'edit message {mid} into the night recap ({len(hits)} tracks, {why}; silent)')
    if DRY:
        print(plain(text))
        for row in (markup or {}).get('inline_keyboard', []):
            print('  [%s] -> %s' % (row[0]['text'], row[0]['callback_data']))
    else:
        try:
            if not edit(mid, text, markup):
                log('recap card %s gone' % mid)
                return False
        except TgError as e:
            log('recap edit: %s' % e.desc)
            return True
        if markup:
            keep_buttons(mid)
    rc['hash'] = h
    return True


def recap_tick(st, now, end=False):
    """An open recap: re-edit on new IDs or crate changes; at its end (or end=True: the next card, `off`) unpin it."""
    rc = st.get('recap')
    if not rc:
        return
    end = end or now >= iso(rc['until'])
    hits = night_hits(iso(rc['since']), iso(rc['until']))
    gone = bool(hits) and not recap_show(rc, hits, 'update')
    if end or gone:
        if rc.get('pinned') and not gone:
            act(f'unpin the recap {rc["message_id"]} by id')
            if not DRY:
                unpin(rc['message_id'])
        st.pop('recap', None)


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ commands
def get_now(a):
    global SIMULATED
    s = getattr(a, 'now', None) or os.environ.get('EVENT_CARD_NOW')
    if s:
        SIMULATED = True
        t = iso(s)
        if not t:
            sys.exit('event-card: bad --now %r (ISO, e.g. 2026-10-22T16:44)' % s)
        return t
    return fixed(dt.datetime.now(TZ)).replace(second=0, microsecond=0)


def load_state():
    st = read_json(STATE_F, {}) or {}
    st.setdefault('done', {})
    st.setdefault('alerts', [])
    return st


def save_state(st, now):
    keep = sorted(st['done'].items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1].get('at', ''))[-20:]
    st['done'] = dict(keep)
    st['alerts'] = st['alerts'][-40:]
    write_json(STATE_F, st)


def act(msg):
    if DRY:
        print('[dry-run] would ' + msg)
    else:
        log(msg)


def finish(st, n, now, why):
    mid = st.get('message_id')
    if st.get('recap'):
        recap_tick(st, now, end=True)             # an older recap still open: close it first
    rc = new_recap(st, n, now, why) if mid and n and why in ('home', 'cutoff') else None
    hits = night_hits(iso(rc['since']), iso(rc['until'])) if rc else None
    shown = recap_show(rc, hits, why) if hits else None
    if shown:
        rc['pinned'] = True                       # the recap stays pinned until its end (recap_tick)
    elif mid:
        text = final_text(n, now, why) if n else '<b>⏹ Live card ended</b>'
        act(f'edit message {mid} (final, {why}) and unpin it by id')
        if DRY:
            print(plain(text))
        else:
            if shown is None:
                try:
                    edit(mid, text)
                except TgError as e:
                    log('final edit: %s' % e.desc)
            unpin(mid)
        if shown is False:                        # the card is gone: no recap
            rc = None
    if rc:
        st['recap'] = rc                          # unpinned: IDs that still come in edit the record into the recap
    key = st.get('night') or (n and n['key'])
    if key:
        st['done'][key] = {'why': why, 'at': now.isoformat()}
    for k in ('night', 'message_id', 'seen_away', 'resends', 'last_hash', 'last_edit', 'conns', 'missed', 'here_at'):
        st.pop(k, None)


def maybe_alert(st, alert, now):
    if not alert or not alert.get('leg'):
        return
    akey = '%s:%s' % (alert['leg'], alert['kind'])
    if akey in st['alerts']:
        return
    if tw_covers(alert['leg'], [k for k in alert['keys'] if k], now):
        return                                   # train-watch's note (→ the session) covers it
    alt = alert.get('alt') or {}
    text = '🔴 ' + esc(alert['line'].replace('🚆 Next: ', '')) + (
        f'\n↪ <a href="{esc(alt["link"])}">{esc(alt.get("text") or "")}</a>' if alt.get('link') else
        (f'\n↪ {esc(alt.get("text"))}' if alt.get('text') else ''))
    act(f'send ONE alert (notifies): {plain(text)}')
    if not DRY:
        try:
            call('sendMessage', text=text, parse_mode='HTML', link_preview_options={'is_disabled': True})
        except TgError as e:
            log('alert failed: %s' % e.desc)
            return
    st['alerts'].append(akey)


def cmd_run(a):
    now = get_now(a)
    st = load_state()
    if st.get('recap') and not st.get('message_id'):
        recap_tick(st, now)
        save_state(st, now)
    events = load_events()
    active = st.get('night') if st.get('message_id') else None
    if not active and not events:
        return 0
    nights = find_nights(events, now)
    if active:
        n = next((x for x in nights if x['key'] == active), None)
        if n is None:
            finish(st, None, now, 'gone')
            save_state(st, now)
            return 0
    else:
        n = next((x for x in nights if x['start'] <= now < x['end'] and x['key'] not in st['done']), None)
        if n is None:
            return 0                              # the cheap exit: no card due
    if now >= n['end']:
        finish(st, n, now, 'cutoff')
        save_state(st, now)
        return 0
    global LAST_PLACE
    LAST_PLACE = place_info()
    kind = place_kind(LAST_PLACE)
    if kind and kind != 'home':
        st['seen_away'] = True
    if kind == 'home' and (st.get('seen_away') or now >= n['ev']['_s']):
        if active:
            finish(st, n, now, 'home')
        else:
            st['done'][n['key']] = {'why': 'home', 'at': now.isoformat()}
            if DRY:
                print('[dry-run] home already after the start: no card tonight')
        save_state(st, now)
        return 0
    here = still_here(LAST_PLACE, n['ev'])
    b = n.get('back')
    if b and here is True and b['_s'] + MISSED_GRACE <= now < b['_e'] and st.get('missed') != n['key']:
        st['missed'] = n['key']                   # he stayed: the card shows the way home, not the planned leg
        lid = tw_leg_ids().get(b.get('id'))       # train-watch's id for it: its notes on this leg are moot now
        if lid:
            ml = {k: v for k, v in (st.get('missed_legs') or {}).items()
                  if (iso(v) or now) > now - MISSED_KEEP}
            ml[lid] = b['_s'].isoformat()
            st['missed_legs'] = ml
        log('%s: still in the venue town after the leg home left' % n['key'])
    if here is True:
        st['here_at'] = now.isoformat()
    text, alert = render(n, now, tw_leg_ids(), missed=st.get('missed') == n['key'], here=here, conns=st.get('conns'),
                         here_at=iso(st.get('here_at')))
    if DRY:
        lt = lambda t, f: t.astimezone(TZ).strftime(f)
        print('[dry-run] %s · %s · window %s–%s' % (lt(now, '%a %d.%m %H:%M'), n['ev'].get('title'),
                                                     lt(n['start'], '%d.%m %H:%M'), lt(n['end'], '%d.%m %H:%M')))
    h = hashlib.sha256(text.encode()).hexdigest()[:16]
    mid = st.get('message_id')
    if mid and h != st.get('last_hash'):
        act(f'edit message {mid} (silent)')
        if not DRY and not edit(mid, text, talk_markup()):   # an edit without the markup would drop the button
            log('card %s gone; sending a new one' % mid)
            mid = None
            st['resends'] = st.get('resends', 0) + 1
    if not mid:
        if st.get('resends', 0) > 3:
            finish(st, n, now, 'off')
            save_state(st, now)
            return 1
        if st.get('recap'):
            recap_tick(st, now, end=True)         # last night's recap makes way for tonight's card
        act('send the card (disable_notification) and pin it silently')
        if not DRY:
            mid = send_card(text)
            st.update(night=n['key'], message_id=mid)
            write_json(STATE_F, st)              # remember it before pinning: no duplicates on a failure below
            if talk_markup():
                keep_buttons(mid)                # a Talk tap (session path) never strips the keyboard
            pin(mid)
            log('sent and pinned card %s' % mid)
    st.update(last_hash=h, last_edit=now.isoformat())
    remember_conns(st, LAST_GH)
    if DRY:
        print(plain(text))
    maybe_alert(st, alert, now)
    save_state(st, now)
    return 0


def cmd_status(a):
    now = get_now(a)
    st = load_state()
    nights = [n for n in find_nights(load_events(), now, rave_check=False) if n['end'] > now]
    rows = [{'title': n['ev'].get('title'), 'town': n['ev'].get('town'), 'start': n['start'].isoformat(),
             'end': n['end'].isoformat(), 'legs': len(n['legs']), 'done': (st['done'].get(n['key']) or {}).get('why'),
             'active': st.get('night') == n['key']} for n in nights[:5]]
    rc = st.get('recap')
    out = {'message_id': st.get('message_id'), 'night': st.get('night'), 'last_edit': st.get('last_edit'),
           'seen_away': bool(st.get('seen_away')), 'upcoming': rows,
           'missed_legs': {k: v for k, v in (st.get('missed_legs') or {}).items()
                           if (iso(v) or now) > now - MISSED_KEEP},
           'recap': {'message_id': rc.get('message_id'), 'night': rc.get('night'), 'until': rc.get('until'),
                     'pinned': bool(rc.get('pinned'))} if rc else None}
    if getattr(a, 'json', False):
        print(json.dumps(out, ensure_ascii=False))
        return 0
    print('Card: %s' % ('message %s, last edit %s' % (st['message_id'], st.get('last_edit'))
                        if st.get('message_id') else 'none live'))
    if rc:
        print('Recap: message %s, %s until %s' % (rc.get('message_id'), 'pinned' if rc.get('pinned') else 'not pinned',
                                                  str(rc.get('until'))[5:16].replace('T', ' ')))
    for r in rows:
        print('- %s (%s): card %s → %s, %d legs%s' % (
            r['title'], r['town'], r['start'][5:16].replace('T', ' '), r['end'][5:16].replace('T', ' '), r['legs'],
            ' · live' if r['active'] else (' · ' + r['done'] if r['done'] else '')))
    if not rows:
        print('No event night with legs in the cache (rave-only nights are found on the day).')
    return 0


def cmd_off(a):
    now = get_now(a)
    st = load_state()
    nights = find_nights(load_events(), now, rave_check=False)
    n = next((x for x in nights if x['key'] == st.get('night')), None)
    if st.get('recap'):
        recap_tick(st, now, end=True)
    if st.get('message_id'):
        finish(st, n, now, 'off')
    else:
        for x in nights:
            if x['start'].date() <= now.date() <= x['end'].date() and x['end'] > now:
                st['done'][x['key']] = {'why': 'off', 'at': now.isoformat()}
    save_state(st, now)
    print('event-card: off for tonight')
    return 0


def main(argv):
    global DRY
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog='event-card', description=__doc__.split('\n')[0])
    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest='cmd')
    r = sub.add_parser('run')
    r.add_argument('--dry-run', action='store_true')
    r.add_argument('--now')
    s = sub.add_parser('status')
    s.add_argument('--json', action='store_true')
    s.add_argument('--now')
    o = sub.add_parser('off')
    o.add_argument('--now')
    a = p.parse_args(argv)
    if not a.cmd:
        print(__doc__.strip())
        return 2
    DRY = bool(getattr(a, 'dry_run', False))
    if a.cmd == 'status':
        return cmd_status(a)
    os.makedirs(DIR, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
    fd = locks.acquire(os.path.join(DIR, '.lock'), wait=0 if a.cmd == 'run' and not DRY else None)
    if fd is None:
        return 0                                  # another run is busy (fd stays open until exit: core.locks)
    try:
        return cmd_run(a) if a.cmd == 'run' else cmd_off(a)
    except (TgError, RuntimeError, OSError) as e:
        print('event-card: %s' % TOKEN_RE.sub('<token>', str(e)), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1


if __name__ == '__main__':
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
